  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nSlightly below normal to near normal temperatures persist t. \nSunday will warm a few degrees compared to Saturday, as our area\ngets a brief period of southwesterly return flow ahead of the \nnext system. Consensus is still good on another cold front, \nweaker than that of Friday, crossing over our area come late \nSunday. This front will bring west/northwest winds and keep the\ncool conditions in place. This trough should keep the tropical \nmoisture from activity in the eastern Pacific south and east of \nour area. Though, just enough of that tropical moisture reaches\nthe area to support a 15-30% chance of showers primarily across\nhigher terrain of southwest Idaho. Shortwave ridging behind \nthis trough will for dry conditions and a warming trend into \nmid-week next week.",
